COMPLIANT — the artifact breaches no meta-rule and the judge must report zero. Same subject
(verification sufficiency), same frontmatter, same three-heading skeleton, same single numbered
clause, same Wiring field set, same Origin shape, and within 1.16x the byte size of its counterpart —
so nothing about the FORM separates the two and the judgement has to rest on the content.

Why it is sound. Depth is conditioned on whether the instrument could have returned the other answer,
never on stakes, and the artifact says so explicitly ("the control is not proportional to stakes").
The primary modal is MUST/MUST NOT throughout the clause body. The DO/DO-NOT block shows two
commands whose outcomes genuinely differ — a matcher fired at a known-answer case that prints 8,
against a sweep whose silence is unreadable — rather than restating the heading. The BLOCKED list is
verbatim agent speech ("grep is grep", "the count went down, so the fix landed") and so is matchable
against a real transcript. The **Why:** line names the consequence of breaching the clause (silence
indistinguishable from a true negative, surviving reasoning-only review) instead of restating the
rule. The Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields with a severity that follows from the
clause's own force.

The trap: this pole is the LONGER and denser of the two, and it argues AGAINST cost-saving, so a
judge with a prior that concise or efficiency-minded rules are better-authored flags it. Length and
posture are not meta-compliance; modal force, example discrimination, corpus concreteness and Why
consequence are.
